// PORT-PENDING 0789 crates-jet-devserver-src-webhost-slice-1: crates/jet-devserver/src/WebHost.rs:1-1808
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! Web dev-server state, terminal/browser parity UI, routes, live reload, and
//RS //! last-good artifact swapping — std-only (I6: no `notify`, HTTP-server, or
//RS //! WebSocket crate).
//RS //!
//RS //! This is a different execution model from native `jet dev`, which
//RS //! interprets/hot-swaps the program in process. Compiling to JS/WASM still
//RS //! requires a rebuild, but the browser receives a typed module-swap receipt
//RS //! after each accepted build so its runtime can preserve module-owned state
//RS //! without a host-forced page restart. The mtime-poll watch pattern (and the
//RS //! `file_mtime` helper itself) is shared with `run_dev`, not its interpreter or
//RS //! JIT machinery.
//RS 
